                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Suppression of cough</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Loperamide is an opioid that is used for diarrhoea because it does not get into the system and does not cause the addivtive euphoric effects of many other opioids.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Loperamide is an opioid that is used for diarrhoea because it does not get into the system and does not cause the addivtive euphoric effects of many other opioids.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Diarrhoea</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>No, most opioids appear ineffective for neuropathic pain, although there are some synthetic 'opioids' like methadone that have additional activity on the NMDA or or other receptors and those may have some positive effects.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Good work!, most opioids appear ineffective for neuropathic pain, although there are some synthetic 'opioids' like methadone that have additional activity on the NMDA or or other receptors and those may have some positive effects.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Neuropathic pain like that from diabetic neuropathy</div>\n"
                }
